METHOD
For every half-level 0<=K<=30 and every half-label 0<=Q,S<=K,
the audit works in the exact integer group ring of the cyclic group
of order L=2K+2.  It constructs

  beta_Q=sum_(t=-Q)^Q z^t,
  A_S=z^S-z^(-S-1),

and compares beta_Q A_S with an independently constructed finite
SU(2) fusion product.  It then compares every cyclic-gradient power

  [z^S] beta_Q^n A_0

with the integer finite-fusion recurrence through n=41, checking the
affine antisymmetry at every cyclic coordinate.

For every even power n=2s, 1<=s<=20, it verifies exactly that the
anchored determinant at radius R is both the cyclic prefix

  d_0 sum_(u=-R)^R delta(S+u)-d_R d_S

and the telescoping sum of its radius shells.  It checks every radius
0<=R<=K.  The restricted counter current count uses 1<=R<=Q; the
all-radius count uses every 0<=R<=K.

The absence of a negative cumulative current is a bounded diagnostic,
not a proof for unbounded K or s.  The exact negative shell and suffix
counts disprove the corresponding termwise and outside-in
strengthenings.  The exact adjacent-minor, shell-recrossing, and chord
counts likewise disprove eventual TP2, a one-crossing shell proof, and
linear interpolation from the simple-current endpoint.  The
log-concavity checks audit the separate unbounded midpoint proof in the
manuscript.

